            "level": {
              "value": 5
            },
            "description": {
              "value": "Your freshly spilled blood is sanctified, and ingesting it causes effects similar to those of holy water\n\nWhenever a fiend, undead, or creature with a weakness to good damage drinks your blood or deals piercing or slashing damage to you with jaws, fangs, or a similar attack, that creature takes 1d6 good damage. You gain a +4 circumstance bonus to Crafting checks to Craft holy water using your own blood as one of the ingredients."
            }
          }
        }
